  "name": "Question 25",
  "problem": "$(-5)\\cdot (3.3)=$",
  "worked_solution": "We have a product of a negative number $(-5)$ and a positive number $(3.3).$ So the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-5)\\cdot 3.3=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $-5$ by $3.3$ without any signs: $5\\cdot 3.3=16.5.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-5)\\cdot 3.3=-16.5.\n$$",
